+# Builder F, build phase 8.4, "answers worth reading"
+
+Four tickets, all decided by the product owner on 2026-09-25 (DECISIONS.md rows of that date). File fence: `synthesis/answer_layout.py`, `synthesis/grounding.py`, `synthesis/trust.py`, `contracts/events.py` (wording only), tests under `tests/system_03_search_agent/synthesis/` and `tests/system_03_search_agent/contracts/`.
+
+## Card 32: the variant-to-disease table says where it comes from
+
+Added `VARIANT_TO_DISEASE_SOURCE_NOTE` (the pinned text, exact) and `variant_to_disease_source_note(entity_type, mapped)` to `synthesis/answer_layout.py`, right after `TABLE_HEADINGS`. Returns the note only for `entity_type == "SequenceVariant"` with `mapped` true, the same two conditions `core/graph.py`'s `listing()` closure already checks before choosing `TABLE_HEADINGS[entity_type]` over the generic "records found" heading, so the note lines up with exactly the table it names.
+
+Tests: `test_the_variant_to_disease_table_names_its_two_sources` (pins the exact string) and `test_the_variant_to_disease_note_is_silent_off_its_own_table` (parametrized over Gene, Clinical trial, Pathogen Detection isolate, an unmapped SequenceVariant, and the empty type, asserting `None` for every one).
+
+WIRING NEEDED IN `core/graph.py`, out of my fence, owned by another builder tonight: in the `listing()` closure, right after the block that computes `mapped` and picks `TABLE_HEADINGS.get(entity_type, records_heading)` (around line 9330 to 9364 on the branch I read), call `variant_to_disease_source_note(entity_type, mapped)` once per table group and append the result (when not `None`) to that table's own note, the same way `placeholder_note` is appended to the answer's `notes` list further down (around line 10567). It must be its own note, scoped to the Variant-to-disease table specifically, not folded into the answer-wide `notes` list unconditionally, since the ticket says "shown only when that table is shown."
+
+## Card 25: a reworded sentence never points at the wrong paper through a generic shared word
+
+`_names_its_record` in `synthesis/grounding.py` used to accept a reworded sentence that switched records on ANY shared content word with that record's title. Fixed with a structural rule, no stop-word list, per the owner's ruling ("Structure, not words"):
+
+A shared word only counts when it does NOT also appear in every OTHER cited record's title in the same answer. `_names_its_record(sentence, labels, other_labels="")` now takes the switched-to record's own title text (`labels`) and every other record's title text in the answer (`other_labels`), and returns true only when `stemmed(sentence) & stemmed(labels)` has at least one word outside `stemmed(other_labels)`. The call site (inside `run_grounding_pass`) now builds `other_labels` from `labels_by_url`, excluding the URLs cited by the current sentence.
+
+This directly fixes the measured residual (`testing/UI_fixes_done.md`, item 12.16 part 4): "patients" sat in a BRCA title and, in the replay, also in the Tay-Sachs title in the same answer, so it names nothing. A genuinely distinguishing word (unique to the record actually being switched to, "BRCA1", "breast", "cancer" in the replay) still licenses the switch.
+
+Tests added to `tests/system_03_search_agent/synthesis/test_sentence_check.py`: `test_a_generic_shared_word_does_not_name_the_switch` (replays the Tay-Sachs/BRCA case, asserts the reworded sentence is dropped) and `test_a_distinguishing_word_still_names_the_switch` (proves the fix is not a blanket ban on switching records). Existing tests (`test_the_switch_rule_can_fail`, `test_naming_the_other_record_instead_of_referring_back_stays`, and the rest of that file) still pass unchanged. Full scoped run: `python3 -m pytest tests/system_03_search_agent/synthesis -q` passes, 661 passed, 10 skipped, 1 xfailed (skips and the one xfail predate this work).
+
+Note for whoever reproduces this kind of case again: the exact substring shortcut through `ground_claim`'s strict path bypasses the switch check entirely (`reworded` only becomes true when the sentence took the quote-anchored synthesis path). A probe that is a literal prefix of its quote never exercises `_names_its_record` at all; the replay test's probe deliberately reworks a word ("carried" to "had") so it takes that path.
+
+## Card 16: the trust line says what is true, calmly
+
+`synthesis/trust.py`'s `answer_trust_line`, the `ask` branch only (the tier logic in `synthesis/trust.py`'s `decide`/`DECISION_TABLE` is untouched):
+
+- Single database: "Based on N source(s) from one database" (was "Based on N source(s), not yet confirmed").
+- Two or more databases (triangulation still came back insufficient, meaning the values could not be shown to agree): "Based on N source(s) from M databases, which differ".
+
+I chose "which differ" for the multi-database `ask` case, per the ticket's own suggested wording. From the user's chair: a reader looking at several sources from several databases that could not be confirmed to agree deserves to be told that plainly rather than "not yet confirmed", which reads as a promise that confirmation is merely pending. "Which differ" is honest without claiming more precision than the system actually computed (Section 8.3.2's bucket comparison, not a raw-value diff).
+
+Updated every pinned assertion of the old text under my fence: `test_trust_line_single_source_not_confirmed` and `test_trust_line_based_on_counts_visible_citations_not_databases` in `tests/system_03_search_agent/synthesis/test_answer_layout.py`. Also reworded the illustrative comment in `contracts/events.py` on `DonePayload.trust_line` (comment only, not a schema change).
+
+NOT IN MY FENCE, flagging rather than fixing: `tests/system_03_search_agent/core/test_layer_handoff.py` line 230 mentions "not yet confirmed" but only in a comment, not an assertion, so it needs no change. Several `frontend/` test files (`answerLayout.test.tsx`, `set9AnswerStructure.test.tsx`, `answerPagination.test.tsx`) pin the OLD wording in fixture data and one assertion (`set9AnswerStructure.test.tsx` lines 116, 224, 229). I did not touch `frontend/`, per my fence. Whoever owns the frontend surface for this phase will need to update those fixtures and that assertion to the new wording, or the frontend suite will show a stale string that no longer matches what the backend emits (though it will not itself fail, since those are fixture literals, not calls into the backend).
