+## Card 26: a record with several sentences shows as one entry, not several list rows
+
+Investigated first, per the ticket's own instruction to report if the cause is elsewhere. It is elsewhere, split across two files, only one of which is in my fence:
+
+- `synthesis/findings.py`'s `build_structured_fallback_narrative` (item 11.34, not in my fence) marks every sentence of a multi-sentence finding value with that SAME finding's `ref_index`, so `run_grounding_pass` grounds each sentence independently instead of losing the whole value to one unreachable trailing marker. This is correct and not the defect; it is why a long abstract survives grounding as several separate grounded sentences that all point at the same citation.
+- `core/graph.py`'s `listing()` closure (not in my fence, owned by another builder tonight) is what actually builds the list rows. It loops `for sentence in sentences: ids = marker_ids(sentence); finding = finding_by_citation_id.get(ids[0]); groups.setdefault(key, []).append((sentence, finding))`, one row PER SURVIVING SENTENCE, with no dedup by citation. A three-sentence abstract that survives grounding as three sentences (all citing the same record) becomes three entries in `groups[key]` and therefore three rows under one heading.
+
+`synthesis/answer_layout.py` itself does none of the row-splitting; it only supplies the per-row label, cell and column helpers `listing()` calls. So the fix that belongs in my fence is a reusable merge function, not a change to the splitting logic itself (there is no splitting logic here to change).
+
+Added `merge_sentences_by_citation(entries)` to `synthesis/answer_layout.py`: collapses a list of `(sentence, finding_or_none)` pairs so that every entry sharing the same `finding.citation_id` becomes ONE entry, its sentences joined with a single space in survival order, keeping the group's first-occurrence position. An entry with `finding is None` (an unmarked framing sentence) is never merged with anything.
+
+Four tests in `tests/system_03_search_agent/synthesis/test_answer_layout.py`: the three-sentence-one-record case, two distinct records staying two entries, an unmarked framing sentence never merging, and a record's later sentence still folding into its FIRST row's position when another record's row sits between them.
+
+WIRING NEEDED IN `core/graph.py`, out of my fence: both `entries = groups[noun]` (around line 9315, the Researcher table/list path) and the loop inside `plain_listing()` (around line 9260, which does not even group first, it walks `sentences` directly) need to run their `(sentence, finding)` pairs through `merge_sentences_by_citation` before building rows. For `plain_listing`, the simplest correct change is to merge the raw `(sentence, finding)` pairs built from `sentences` before the `for sentence in sentences:` loop that emits `sentence_token`. For the Researcher path, `entries = merge_sentences_by_citation(groups[noun])` right where `entries = groups[noun]` is assigned.
+
